From 5f96b4aa024d8950a7addd03d5e45b253fe69412 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Scheduikat <luantak@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] link: compact tiny panic origin tables

Reversible tiny panic sites need PC-to-file mappings, but retaining the
original CU tables also retains holes for dead code and copies the same
physical filename placeholder many times. Use one dense global file table
and rewrite file PC data to its indices without changing shared symbols.

Omit file PC data with no opaque sites, merge adjacent hidden ranges, and
deduplicate rewritten tables. Store only each token hash; the tiny panic
printer restores the common prefix and suffix. Default-mode tables and
execution metadata remain unchanged.

On the existing tiny fixture with Go 1.27.0 and seed AAAAAAAAAAA, this
reduces the binary from 2,683,004 to 2,494,588 bytes. The generic-diagnostic
baseline is 2,211,964 bytes. Panic-origin reversal and stripped public
source-location APIs pass in the focused non-short fixture.

Refs burrowers/garble#604.
